    <article>
      <p class="legal-lede">{{ site.legal.controllerName }} (“ScratchBox”, “we”, “us” or “our”) is responsible for this website. Our contact point for privacy requests is <a href="mailto:{{ site.legal.contactEmail }}">{{ site.legal.contactEmail }}</a>. We operate from {{ site.legal.location }}.</p>
      <h2 id="collection">What we collect</h2><p>We collect information you provide in an enquiry, including your name, work email, company, website, role, phone number, industry, business objective, revenue range, investment range, timeline and message. We also collect technical and campaign information such as IP-related device data, browser and page activity, referral URLs, UTM parameters and advertising click identifiers where you allow non-essential tracking.</p>
      <h2 id="use">How we use information</h2><p>We use enquiry information to respond to you, assess fit, prepare a proposal, manage our relationship, protect the website and improve our services. We use analytics and campaign information to understand website performance, measure advertising and improve communications. We do not use your information for decisions that produce legal or similarly significant effects without human involvement.</p>
      <h2 id="cookies">Cookies, analytics and advertising choices</h2><p>Necessary storage supports essential website functions. With your choice, we may use Google Analytics, Microsoft Clarity, Meta Pixel and, where configured, LinkedIn Insight Tag to measure traffic, understand interactions and measure advertising. These providers may receive online identifiers, device/browser data, pages viewed and campaign information. Under some US state laws, disclosures to ad platforms for cross-context behavioural advertising may be considered “sharing”.</p><p>You can accept, reject or change non-essential tracking through <button class="legal-text-button" type="button" onclick="openPrivacyChoices()">Privacy Choices</button>. We honour a browser Global Privacy Control signal by disabling marketing tracking. We do not sell personal information for money.</p>
      <h2>Who receives information</h2><p>We share data only as needed with service providers that support hosting, database and CRM operations, analytics, advertising measurement, communications and professional services. Current website measurement providers include Google, Microsoft Clarity and Meta; WhatsApp may process data when you choose to contact us there. We may disclose information where required by law or to protect rights, safety and security.</p>
      <h2>International transfers and retention</h2><p>Our service providers may process information in India and other countries where they operate. We retain enquiry and prospect records for as long as needed to manage the enquiry and relationship, normally no more than 24 months after the last meaningful interaction, unless a longer period is required for a contract, legal obligation, dispute or security purpose. We then delete or anonymise the information where practical.</p>
      <h2 id="rights">Your privacy rights</h2><p>Depending on where you live, you may ask to access, correct, delete, restrict or object to processing of your information, withdraw consent, receive a portable copy, or opt out of certain advertising-related sharing. California residents may have rights to know, delete, correct and opt out of sale/sharing. We will verify requests and respond within applicable legal timeframes. To make a request, email <a href="mailto:{{ site.legal.contactEmail }}">{{ site.legal.contactEmail }}</a> with the subject line “Privacy Request”.</p>
      <h2>Country-specific information</h2><p><strong>India:</strong> this notice describes the personal data and purposes of processing, and you can withdraw consent or make a rights request using the contact above. <strong>Switzerland:</strong> we provide this notice to explain the controller, data, purposes, recipients, retention and cross-border processing. <strong>UAE:</strong> where consent is required, we seek it through our consent controls and process requests through the contact above. <strong>United States:</strong> this notice is also intended to serve as a notice at collection where applicable; use Privacy Choices to opt out of non-essential advertising tracking.</p>
      <h2>Security and children</h2><p>We use reasonable technical and organisational safeguards designed to protect personal information. No online system is completely secure. This website is not directed to children and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children.</p>
      <h2>Changes</h2><p>We may update this policy when our practices or legal obligations change. We will post the revised policy and update the effective date.</p>
      <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2><p>For privacy questions, requests or complaints, contact <a href="mailto:{{ site.legal.contactEmail }}">{{ site.legal.contactEmail }}</a>. You may also have the right to contact your local data-protection authority.</p>
